  "description": "Online return after a service visit (streaming): as in vehicle_in_service_ends_drive two D polls start a drive and vehicle_in_service closes it and disconnects the stream, but the vehicle then comes back online parked (30 s later) instead of asleep; from :start that return is a probe followed by the strict fetch, so a second parked payload settles the terminal. The in-service branch leaves stream_pid set, so the :start online handler takes it for a live stream and does not connect a new one: the interactions section ends with the disconnect after serve 4 and shows no connect after serve 5 \u2014 the car runs without its stream until the next drive reconnects it (#5742). This pins today's behaviour; after the fix a connect after serve 5 is expected. One open online row, one closed drive, state topic online, driving, start, online. The online terminal repeats without writing; no await, because close_drive runs on the error serve and the online start on the return serve, before the terminal.",
